WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.485
As countries move through the global stocktake
under the Paris Agreement,

00:00:04.565 --> 00:00:08.863
they need to know where the carbon is going right
now, not a year ago.

00:00:08.943 --> 00:00:13.554
The existing databases of ocean carbon fluxes are
detailed and trustworthy,

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:16.368
but they are always looking backward in time.

00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:20.996
What is missing is a way to bring that same rigor
up to the present month,

00:00:21.076 --> 00:00:26.750
so that policymakers and scientists can respond to
changes in the ocean sink as they happen.
